Q: Add Parent and Child entity in the same context.SaveChanges A: <p>I'm making a few assumptions here - they do match a large number of scenarios, possibly yours as well. If those assumptions are <em>wrong</em> - you'll need to adjust to your specific setup.</p>
<ul>
<li>You have a navigation property in your <code>Parent</code> class to hold the child object</li>
<li>Using SQL Server as the database</li>
<li>Using <code>IDENTITY</code> primary keys in your tables</li>
</ul>
<p>In that case: adding a new entry to the database using</p>
<pre><code>var entry = _context.LookupItems.Add(item);
</code></pre>
<p>does <strong>NOT</strong> create a new <code>Id</code> value - you're not really adding the record to the database, just to your context (in memory).</p>
<p>The way to handle this is:</p>
<ul>
<li>Create the new parent object</li>
<li>Create the new child object, and assign it to a navigation property</li>
<li>Save the complete object graph at once, and let EF Core handle all the nitty gritty details of fixing up the <code>Id</code> values upon inserting the rows into the database table.</li>
</ul>
<p>Try this code:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>// Create new parent object - as is 
Parent newParent = new Parent();
newParent.Name = &quot;myName&quot;;

// Create new child object
LookupItem item = new LookupItem();
item.data= &quot;test&quot;;

// Assign new child object to parent
newParent.lookup = item;

// Now save complete object graph to context 
_context.Parents.Add(newParent);

// Persist changes made to database
await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
</code></pre>
